<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <title>PUP ITECH FEEDBACK SYSTEM</title>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="style1.css">
    </head>

    <body>
         
<div id="header">
  <img src="images/pup_logo.png" alt="PUP_Logo">
  <img src="images/itech_logo.png" alt="ITECH_Logo">
  <h1 id="title">PUP INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY</h1>
  <div id="nav">
    <button onclick="showSection('homediv')">Home</button>
    <button onclick="showSection('resultdiv')">Results</button>
    <button onclick="showSection('aboutdiv')">About Us</button>
  </div>
</div>

<div id="homediv" class="section active">

  <div id="homecontent">

    <h2>Home</h2> <br>
    <p>Welcome to the ITECH student Feedback Portal, a dedicated space for every
      student to share their insights and experiences regarding our learning
      environment. At the Institute of Technology, we believe that your voice is the
      most vital tool for institutional growth, and we are committed to ensuring that
      every concern-form is state of our facilities and classroom cleanliness to
      academic experiences-is heard and addressed. By participating in this survey,
      you are taking an active role in shaping a better, more efficient, and more
      supportive department for yourself and your fellow students. Your honest
      feedback is the foundation upon which we will build a stronger community,
      turning individual observations into collective progress for our second home.</p>


  </div>
</div>
<div id="resultdiv" class="section">
<div id="resultdiv" class="section">
    <div id="resultscontent">
        <h2>Survey Results</h2>
        <br>
        <!-- This is where your table will appear -->
        <table border="1" id="responsesTable" style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left;">
            <thead>
                <tr style="background-color: #800000; color: white;">
                    <th style="padding: 10px;">Name</th>
                    <th style="padding: 10px;">Email</th>
                    <th style="padding: 10px;">Time Submitted</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="tableBody">
                <!-- Data from Firebase will be injected here -->
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="surveydiv" class="section">

  <div id="surveycontent">
    <h1>STUDENT FEEDBACK FORM</h1>
    <h3>Personal Information</h3>
    <hr>
    <label>Name: </label>
    <input type="text" id="name" name="name"><br>
    <label>Email Address: </label>
    <input type="email" id="email" name="email"><br>
    <label><input type="checkbox" id="anon" name="anonymous">Stay Anonymous</label>

  </div>

  <div id="surveycontent2">

    <form id="question1">

      <h3>Experience Rating</h3>
      <hr>

      <p>1. Do you experience any issues in your classroom environment (temperature, ventilation, and facilities)?</p>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c1" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox1">Classroom is too hot</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c2" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox2">Classroom is too cold</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c3" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox3">Air conditioning is not working properly</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c4" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox4">Insufficient electric fans</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c5" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox5">Poor ventilation / air circulation</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c6" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox6">Poor lighting (too dim)</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c7" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox7">Lighting is too bright / uncomfortable</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c8" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox8">Flickering or broken lights</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c9" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox9">Overcrowded classroom</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c10" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox10">Not enough chairs or tables</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c11" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox11">Uncomfortable seating (chairs/desks)</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c12" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox12"> Limited space for movement</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c13" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox13">Dirty or poorly maintained classroom</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c14" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox14">Unpleasant smell in the classroom</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c15" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox15">Classroom is comfortable (no issues)</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q1c16" name="issues[]" value="question1checkbox16">Other (please specify): <input type="text" name="issues_other"></label>

    </form>

    <form id="question2">
      <p>2. What is your favorite hangout spot in ITech? What makes it your favorite?</p>
      <label><input type = "radio" id = "q2c1" name = "q2r1" value = "question2radio1">Hallway</label>
      <label><input type = "radio" id = "q2c2" name = "q2r1" value = "question2radio2">First-floor facade area</label>
      <label><input type = "radio" id = "q2c3" name = "q2r1" value = "question2radio3">Library area</label>
      <label><input type = "radio" id = "q2c4" name = "q2r1" value = "question2radio4">Bench areas</label>
      <label><input type = "radio" id = "q2c5" name = "q2r1" value = "question2radio5">Other (please specify): <input type="text" name="q2r1_other"></label>
      <br>
      <p>Factors for Preference (Check all that apply):</p>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c5" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox1">Good ventilation / windy atmosphere</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c6" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox2">Spacious area</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c7" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox3">Less crowded</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c8" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox4">Quiet environment</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c9" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox5">Charging outlets available</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c10" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox6">Strong internet or mobile signal</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c11" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox7">Shade / protection from heat</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c12" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox8">Social freedom / comfortable for group activities</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q2c13" name="preference[]" value="question2checkbox9">Other (please specify): <input type="text" name="preference_other"></label>
    </form>
 

    <form id="question3">
      <p>3. In your opinion, what is the most important improvement needed for the computer laboratory?</p>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c1" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox1">Upgrade or improve computer performance</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c2" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox2">Better and more stable internet connection</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c3" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox3">More chairs and tables</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c4" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox4">Better seating arrangement</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c5" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox5">Increase number of fully working computers</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c6" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox6">Repair or replace defective computers</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c7" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox7">Install updated software and applications</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c8" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox8">Improve availability of required tools/programs</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q3c9" name="improvement[]" value="question3checkbox9">Other (please specify):<input type="text" name="improvement_other"></label>
    </form>

    <form id="question4">
      <p>4. What are the common challenges you encounter during laboratory or workshop activities?</p>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c1" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox1">Lack of personal laptop</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c2" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox2">Not allowed or unable to use laboratory computers</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c3" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox3">Limited number of available computers</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c4" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox4">Computers are not functioning properly</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c5" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox5">Computers lack necessary applications/software</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c6" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox6">Insufficient electrical outlets</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c7" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox7">Some electrical outlets are not working</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c8" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox8">Overcrowded laboratory room</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c9" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox9">Poor ventilation</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c10" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox10">Uncomfortable working environment</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c11" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox11">Unstable internet connection</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="q4c12" name="challenges[]" value="question4checkbox12">Other (please specify): <input type="text" name="challenges_other"></label>


    </form>

    <form id="question5">

      <p>5. The comfort rooms are consistently clean and well-maintained by the staff.</p>

      <label><input type="radio" id="q5c1" name="q5r1" value="question5radio1">Strongly Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q5c2" name="q5r1" value="question5radio2">Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q5c3" name="q5r1" value="question5radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q5c4" name="q5r1" value="question5radio4">Agree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q5c5" name="q5r1" value="question5radio5">Strongly Agree</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question6">
      <p>6. All CR fixtures (toilet handles, drains, faucets) are in good working condition.</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q6c1" name="q6r2" value="question6radio1">Strongly Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q6c2" name="q6r2" value="question6radio2">Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q6c3" name="q6r2" value="question6radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q6c4" name="q6r2" value="question6radio4">Agree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q6c5" name="q6r2" value="question6radio5">Strongly Agree</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question7">
      <p>7. The layout of the comfort rooms provides sufficient privacy and space for students.</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q7c1" name="q7r3" value="question7radio1">Strongly Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q7c2" name="q7r3" value="question7radio2">Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q7c3" name="q7r3" value="question7radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q7c4" name="q7r3" value="question7radio4">Agree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q7c5" name="q7r3" value="question7radio5">Strongly Agree</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question8">
      <p>8. There is always a sufficient supply of water and plastic dippers (tabo) available inside the comfort rooms.</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q8c1" name="q8r4" value="question8radio1">Strongly Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q8c2" name="q8r4" value="question8radio2">Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q8c3" name="q8r4" value="question8radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q8c4" name="q8r4" value="question8radio4">Agree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q8c5" name="q8r4" value="question8radio5">Strongly Agree</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question9">
      <p>9. In general, how would you rate the instructors' ability to explain complex topics in simple, easy-to-understand terms?</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q9c1" name="q9r5" value="question9radio1">Very Poor</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q9c2" name="q9r5" value="question9radio2">Poor</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q9c3" name="q9r5" value="question9radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q9c4" name="q9r5" value="question9radio4">Excellent</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q9c5" name="q9r5" value="question9radio5">Very Excellent</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question10">
      <p>10. On average, to what extent do instructors across the department stay focused on curriculum-related subject matter rather than unrelated topics?</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q10c1" name="q10r6" value="question10radio1">Never</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q10c2" name="q10r6" value="question10radio2">Rarely</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q10c3" name="q10r6" value="question10radio3">Sometimes</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q10c4" name="q10r6" value="question10radio4">Often</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q10c5" name="q10r6" value="question10radio5">Always</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question11">
      <p>11.  To what extent do you agree that the faculty demonstrates strong work ethics and consideration for students' diverse situations?</p>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q11c1" name="q11r7" value="question11radio1">Strongly Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q11c2" name="q11r7" value="question11radio2">Disagree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q11c3" name="q11r7" value="question11radio3">Neutral</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q11c4" name="q11r7" value="question11radio4">Agree</label>
      <label><input type="radio" id="q11c5" name="q11r7" value="question11radio5">Strongly Agree</label>
    </form>

    <form id="question12">
      <p>12. What specific changes would you suggest the department implement to make teaching methods more student-centered and less stressful?</p>
      <label><input type="text" id="q12c1" name="q12c1" placeholder="Type here..."></label>
    </form>

    <button id="submitbtn" class="surveybtn" type="submit">Submit</button>

  </div>
</div>
<div id="aboutdiv" class="section">
  <div id="aboutcontent">

    <h2>About Us</h2> <br>
    <p>We are a dedicated group of five Information Technology students from PUP
       Institute of Technology (ITECH), currently collaborating on this project as part
       of our Web Development course under the guidance of our professor, Ms.
       Jonnalyn Apsay. Out team is composed of Jhon Carl Gabarda, Ryan Libres, Spike
       Palagam, John Marvin Soleybar, Euan Alfonso Suba, and John Felix Sungahid.
       Driven by the principles of user-centered design, our primary mission is to
       create and maintain a digital environment where the voices of our fellow
       students are not only heard but serve as a catalyst for meaningful change. We
       recognize that a better campus starts with open communication, and we are
       committed to providing a transparent, accessible platform that bridges the gap
       between student concerns and departmental improvement.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<button id = "surveybtn" class="surveybtn" onclick="showSection('surveydiv')">SUBMIT A FEEDBACK</button>

<script type="module" src="script1.js"></script>
    </body>

</html>
